{"id": "en_quake_home_p1", "total": 65.31, "segments": [{"text": "If an earthquake hits your home at night, do not run outside into the dark.", "start": 0.0, "end": 2.9}, {"text": "The ground beneath Mark shakes violently, and the walls begin to groan and crack loudly.", "start": 4.0, "end": 7.82}, {"text": "Falling objects and debris near buildings cause most injuries during sudden structural movement events.", "start": 8.64, "end": 12.5}, {"text": "Mark stays completely away from windows, glass, and tall furniture that might fall.", "start": 13.131, "end": 16.48}, {"text": "One. Drop to your hands and knees immediately before the violent shaking knocks you down.", "start": 17.26, "end": 20.86}, {"text": "Two. Cover your head and neck securely under a sturdy wooden table right beside you.", "start": 21.46, "end": 25.08}, {"text": "Three. Hold on tightly to the furniture legs while the violent tremor shakes the house.", "start": 25.54, "end": 29.04}, {"text": "After the violent shaking stops completely, Mark must expect dangerous aftershocks very soon.", "start": 29.56, "end": 33.98}, {"text": "He carefully checks the air around him for any strong gas smell in the room.", "start": 34.52, "end": 37.62}, {"text": "He remembers to leave the building immediately if he smells leaking gas anywhere nearby.", "start": 38.1, "end": 41.28}, {"text": "The heavy tremors finally fade away, leaving a strange and heavy silence in the dark.", "start": 42.0, "end": 45.82}, {"text": "Mark stands up slowly and breathes out a long breath of pure relief tonight.", "start": 46.52, "end": 49.88}, {"text": "He checks his phone for any emergency alerts, but the screen stays completely dark.", "start": 50.52, "end": 53.68}, {"text": "It was the perfect survival plan executed with absolute calm and total precision.", "start": 54.26, "end": 58.06}, {"text": "There was just one unexpected problem waiting for him outside the front door.", "start": 58.06, "end": 62.16}], "words": [["If", 0.0, 0.3